# Generated attribution files (sbom/*.cdx.json, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html) have their
# e-mail addresses masked — and NOTHING else waived. cargo-cyclonedx embeds
# `path+file:///Users/<user>/…` purls for workspace crates, so a release cut on a laptop
# names its owner in every SBOM. Turning the mask into a blanket waiver hides exactly that;
# the sbom/dirty.cdx.json fixture catches it.
file: scripts/lib/residue-gate.py
test: test-residue-gate
---OLD---
    if is_attribution(path):
        # Third-party authors' addresses are the file's purpose, not residue. Mask them so
---NEW---
    if is_attribution(path):
        return []
        # Third-party authors' addresses are the file's purpose, not residue. Mask them so
